# Agent tooling and scratch — must never be committed. Directory patterns do
# not cover the instruction files agents look for at the repo root, so those
# are listed by name; anything project-relevant belongs in a normal doc or in
# the script that enforces it, not in a tool-specific file.
#
# A name blocklist always lags the tooling, so the pre-commit hook installed by
# .github/scripts/install-hooks.sh is the real guard — this list is the cheap
# first line, not the last one.
.claude/
.codex/
.continue/
.cursor/
.github/instructions/
.opencode/
.amazonq/
.augment/
.devin/
.github/prompts/
.goose/
